# Wave W17-AA (Route 220): long rock — swell-shadow rock: a dark blue-grey boulder standing in the long sea, its joints drawn long, foam collar thin at its base — the lane’s only furniture (design: the lane loops wide into open sea; the rocks are few and far between). The baked water is the shipped sea entire — the depth is carried by the boulder’s shadowed face, never by a mismatched water square. Route 220’s own rock — split from its twin Route 219’s jetty rock by face entire (swell-shadow dark vs shallows warm) and from Route 223’s cliff rock ahead of the program by jointing: swell-worn smooth here, cliff-vertical there.
